<title>INDIA: TABLE-India JK Corp makes losses in 96/97.</title>
<headline>TABLE-India JK Corp makes losses in 96/97.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	   (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net (loss) profit	     (178.7)  vs     515.7</p>
<p>    Net sales			7,251.4   vs   6,808.1</p>
<p>    Other income		     220.0   vs     175.0</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)		    1.0   vs	 3.0</p>
<p>    Interest			   875.9   vs     585.3</p>
<p>    Total Expenditure	    6,387.4   vs   5,620.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation		     386.8   vs     257.7</p>
<p>    Tax				    nil   vs	 nil</p>
<p>Note - JK Corporation Ltd managing director Bharat Singhania said poor market conditions hit operations for the three main products -- paper, cement and sythetic yarns.</p>
<p>He said the firm has invested 11 billion rupees to expand capacities and secure economies of scale and reduce costs.</p>
<p>Sales in the first quarter of 1997/98 were up about nine percent, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
